From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:57:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Add the AOP accelerometer and
 gyroscope services

The T8132 firmware sends accelerometer and gyroscope samples (soc: apple:
aop registers both services, 3cadfe50e1), and aop_motion binds to an AOP
child named accel or gyro. Add the two children, disabled, as T604x
describes them; the bootloader fills in their calibration properties from
the Apple device tree. No board enables them here.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 15cb0a8ebd..86fba79ac9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -1350,6 +1350,17 @@
 				compatible = "apple,t8132-aop-las", "apple,aop-las";
 				status = "disabled";
 			};
+
+			/* The calibration properties come from the bootloader. */
+			aop_accel: accel {
+				compatible = "apple,t8132-aop-accel", "apple,aop-accel";
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
+
+			aop_gyro: gyro {
+				compatible = "apple,t8132-aop-gyro", "apple,aop-gyro";
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
 		};
 
 		/* ADT lists the interrupts as 1, 0, 3, 2 of the block: send-empty is the lowest. */
